// Which category DOMINATES the graph? Returns its name, or null.
//
// This is the "Split out" setting's detector. It is deliberately NOT hard-coded to
// "Mortgage" — a category is dominant if it is a large enough share of total spend
// that it flattens everything else, whatever it happens to be called. Rent, school
// fees and a car loan all do the same thing to the scale.
//
